Title: THE WINTER DISPATCH
Author: Claire Montgomery
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


INT. RESISTANCE SAFE HOUSE - LYON - NIGHT - 1943

MARIE DUBOIS hides a SEALED ENVELOPE under the floor. LUC watches the street.
MARIE
The courier comes at dawn. No one opens the door.

INT. GERMAN FIELD OFFICE - DAY

HAUPTMANN STRASSER studies Marie's sketch. A bent BICYCLE wheel sits on his desk.
STRASSER
She uses the market on Rue Victor Hugo.

EXT. LYON MARKET - MORNING

Marie sells herbs. BAKER ANTOINE passes a warning in her basket.
ANTOINE
They searched the canal house yesterday.

INT. SAFE HOUSE - NIGHT

Luc reads a map by candlelight. Marie loads bread and the envelope into a satchel.
LUC
We take the river road. Strasser won't expect it.

INT. CHURCH BASEMENT - NIGHT

FATHER REYNAUD, 60s, blesses three couriers. Marie kneels briefly.
REYNAUD
God keep the names you carry safer than our walls.

EXT. CANAL PATH - NIGHT

Marie and Luc ride the bicycle through fog. Distant engines grow louder.
MARIE
If they stop us, you run.

EXT. RIVER ROAD CHECKPOINT - NIGHT

German soldiers wave down a farm cart ahead. Luc slows.
LUC
We cut through the orchard. Now.

EXT. ORCHARD - NIGHT

They abandon the bicycle and run. A flashlight sweeps the trees.
MARIE
The envelope stays dry. That's all that matters.

INT. FARMHOUSE KITCHEN - NIGHT

MADAME CLAIRE, 70s, hides them behind a pantry wall. Boots crunch outside.
CLAIRE
Strasser pays for whispers. I charge nothing for silence.

EXT. FARM LANE - DAWN

Marie hands the SEALED ENVELOPE to a YOUNG PRIEST on a mule cart. The sun breaks over the hills.
MARIE
Tell London the list is real. Tell them we are still here.

FADE OUT.


THE END
